 "preferred_name": "Non-Facility Associated Signalling",
 "kind": "knowledge",
 "definition": "An ISDN primary rate interface arrangement in which a single D channel carries the signalling for several PRI trunk groups.",
 "description": {
  "text": "A Primary Rate Interface configuration in which multiple T1 carriers share one signaling channel (D channel). A single Primary Rate ISDN circuit normally has 23 bearer channels plus one D channel; NFAS lets several circuits share a D channel.",
